    "field": "Terrestrial carbon cycle modeling",
    "problem": "Simplified representations of processes like forest distribution and carbon allocation in Earth system models (ESMs) contribute to large biases and uncertainty in projections of extratropical forest biomass, hindering accurate carbon stock estimates.",
    "method": "We evaluate forest biomass from eight Earth System Models by comparing simulations against a synthesized remote sensing and ground-based observational dataset to quantify uncertainties in forest distribution, carbon allocation, and pre-industrial vegetation conditions.",
    "task": "The task is to quantify the uncertainty of extratropical forest biomass in CMIP5 models by comparing simulations with observation-based data for the Northern Hemisphere to identify sources of model biases.",
